    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44046" root="&#xA;                        نعم&#xA;                    " body-key="n1">
                        
                            5
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَنَعَّمَ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>he enjoyed,</i> or <i>led, an easy, a
pleasant, a soft,</i> or <i>a delicate, life, with ampleness of the means of subsistence; a life of ease
and plenty.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَنَعَّمَ</span>
                        <i>It</i> (a tree) <i>became
flourishing and fresh,</i> (TK, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">روى</span>, &amp;c.,)
<i>luxuriant, succulent, sappy, soft, tender, and
supple.</i> See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَوِىَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَنَعَّمَ</span>
                        <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَتَّعَ</span>. (Msb. *)

